    {
      "id": "sol.ahsme-1954-p44.live",
      "kind": "proof-sketch",
      "text": "The year \\(x^2\\) must lie in the nineteenth century, so \\(x=43\\) because \\(43^2=1849\\) while the neighboring squares fall outside the relevant range. His birth year is therefore \\[ x^2-x=1849-43=1806, \\] which is in the first half of the century.\n\nThus, the correct answer is E.",
      "hints": [
        "His birth year is \\(x^2-x\\)",
        "Use the requirement that \\(x^2\\) is a nineteenth-century year and test the nearby integer \\(x\\)"
      ],
